element.markdown:
**element** *nameClass* `{` *pattern* `}` — [Spec](https://relaxng.org/compact-tutorial-20030326.html#id2814100)

Defines an element pattern that matches an XML element. The *nameClass* specifies which element names match, and the *pattern* describes the allowed content.

A *nameClass* can be a simple name (`element root { ... }`), a choice (`element (a | b) { ... }`), a wildcard (`element * { ... }`), or a wildcard with exclusions (`element * - local:* { ... }`).

**Examples:**
```rnc
element root { text }
element name { xsd:string }
element (bold | italic) { text }
```

element.plaintext:
element nameClass { pattern }

Defines an element pattern that matches an XML element. The nameClass specifies which element names match, and the pattern describes the allowed content.

See https://relaxng.org/compact-tutorial-20030326.html#id2814100

attribute.plaintext:
attribute nameClass { pattern }

Defines an attribute pattern that matches an XML attribute. The nameClass specifies which attribute names match, and the pattern describes the allowed value.

See https://relaxng.org/compact-tutorial-20030326.html#id2814218

list.plaintext:
list { pattern }

Matches a whitespace-separated list of tokens.

See https://relaxng.org/compact-tutorial-20030326.html#id2816748

mixed.markdown:
**mixed** `{` *pattern* `}` — [Spec](https://relaxng.org/compact-tutorial-20030326.html#id2816748)

Allows mixed content: text interspersed with child elements matching the inner *pattern*. Equivalent to `(text | pattern)*`.

**Examples:**
```rnc
element p {
  mixed {
    element b { text }*
    & element i { text }*
  }
}
```

mixed.plaintext:
mixed { pattern }

Allows mixed content: text interspersed with child elements. Equivalent to (text | pattern)*.

See https://relaxng.org/compact-tutorial-20030326.html#id2816748

include.plaintext:
include anyURILiteral [ { grammarContent } ]

include (reference):
Merges definitions from another RNC grammar file into the current grammar.
  include "inline.rnc"

include { } (override):
Includes a grammar and overrides specific definitions. Definitions inside the body replace the corresponding definitions from the included file.
  include "inline.rnc" {
    paragraph = element p { text }
  }

See https://relaxng.org/compact-tutorial-20030326.html#id2820475

include-override.markdown:
**include** *anyURILiteral* `{` *grammarContent* `}` (override) — [Spec](https://relaxng.org/compact-tutorial-20030326.html#id2820475)

Includes a grammar file and overrides specific definitions. Definitions inside the body replace the corresponding definitions from the included file.

Only names that exist in the included file can be overridden — other names produce an error.

**Example:**
```rnc
include "inline.rnc" {
  paragraph = element p { text }
}
```

div.markdown:
**div** `{` *grammarContent* `}` — [Spec](https://relaxng.org/compact-tutorial-20030326.html#id2820694)

Groups grammar definitions for organizational purposes. Has no semantic effect — `div` blocks are transparent and their contents are treated as if written directly at the enclosing level.

**Examples:**
```rnc
div {
  heading = element h1 { text }
  paragraph = element p { text }
}
```

