grammar.markdown:
**grammar** `{` *grammarContent* `}` — [Spec](https://relaxng.org/compact-tutorial-20030326.html#id2820694)

Defines an explicit grammar block containing `start` and named definitions. Every RNC file is implicitly a grammar, so `grammar { ... }` is mainly used for nested grammars.

A nested grammar creates a new scope for definitions and has its own `start` pattern. Use `parent` to reference the enclosing grammar's definitions.

**Examples:**
```rnc
element root {
  grammar {
    start = element child { parent content }
  }
}
```

grammar.plaintext:
grammar { grammarContent }

Defines an explicit grammar block with its own start pattern and definitions.

See https://relaxng.org/compact-tutorial-20030326.html#id2820694

parent.markdown:
**parent** *name* — [Spec](https://relaxng.org/compact-tutorial-20030326.html#id2820694)

References a named definition in the parent grammar when used inside a nested `grammar { ... }` block.

**Examples:**
```rnc
common = text
start = element root {
  grammar {
    start = element child { parent common }
  }
}
```
